Z||000024||DaRkLoRD||11-16-2001||12:57 PM||||The only movie I actually regretted seeing in the theater, was Jurassic Park 2.. the book was good, the movie was horrible. I might have to see JP3 though, Linda Park is in it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I didn't like Event Horizon either, it wasn't a bad movie, I just didn't like it.<P>Several movies I've rented, I've stopped, rewound and taken back without finishing, cause they were so boring. 2001 was one of them.... <P>and to be honest.. I thought the original Gone in 60 Seconds was pretty bad too. not to mention almost every sci fi movie before the 80s..<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||8
Z||000025||LZeitgeist||11-16-2001||01:09 PM||||<B>Hudson Hawk</B>, with Bruce Willis and Sandra Bernhardt... man, what a waste of time.<P><B>Driven</B>, with Sylvester Stallone, some other dude, and some breasts attached to some chick. Breasts, good. Film, bad.<P><B>Grand Canyon</B> with Steve Martin and Danny Glover was pretty slow and quite possibly the most depressing film I'd ever chosen to see, but the soundtrack has a few good songs on it.<P><B>75% of Jim Carrey's movies.</B> 'The Mask' was great, and he was awesome as The Riddler in whatever Batman movie that was. But the rest of them just pay Jim Carrey to act like Jim Carrey (i.e, like a wanna-be Jerry Lewis, who I don't like either) and they try to write a plot around him. Waste of time.<P><B>Every movie Tom Green has ever done, and every movie he will ever do unless it's a snuff film</B> - just when you thought Jim Carrey acted like a complete and utter moron, guess who comes along...<P><BR>Hey Formula88 - I've been hearing about those films you mentioned for ten years now... pick some new ones already.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
