Z||000029||LZeitgeist||11-16-2001||03:51 PM||||Yup - in The Mask, at least the character he was doing was wacky for a reason, not just an idiot in general. He fit the character he was playing, and the role wasn't created for him. <P>And in the Batman film (Batman Returns, I think?), I thought he did an incredible job as the Riddler - as Edward Nigma, he was so-so, but once in the Riddler persona, he was awesome. I never thought anyone could do as great a job as Frank Gorshin, but Jim Carrey was up to the task. And again, this was not a role that was created for him.<P>Seems like all his other movies are the type where they say, "Hey, we've got Jim Carrey signed.. let's have him do funny stuff and we'll somehow attempt to build a plot around his funnyness." Zzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzz... el suck-o grande.  (IMHO, YMMV.)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
